# The .NET images (Smx.Backend) use this whole `src/` tree as their build
# context. Without this, az acr build uploads every bin/obj/node_modules folder — build output the
# multi-stage Dockerfiles restore fresh anyway. (The frontend keeps its own smx-web/.dockerignore.)
#
# NO TRAILING SLASHES, and keep every form below. `az acr build` does not use docker's matcher: it
# walks FILES and fnmatches each relative path against these patterns, so `**/node_modules/` matched
# the directory entry and nothing inside it — every file under it was still uploaded. That is not
# theoretical. It is why a 6 MB source tree went up as a 190 MiB tarball and timed the deploy out
# on `Read timed out. (read timeout=300)`. The bare forms are the ones smx-web/.dockerignore has
# always used, and that build has always been small.
bin
obj
node_modules
dist
.vs
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vs
**/bin/*
**/obj/*
**/node_modules/*
**/dist/*
**/.vs/*
